# Laravel Team Coding Standards

Stack: Laravel 11+, Inertia.js, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, MySQL.

## Request flow — never skip a layer

```
Route → FormRequest → Controller → Service → Repository → Model
                          ↓
                      Resource
```

| Layer | Does | Never does |
|---|---|---|
| Controller | Receives request, calls service, returns response | Runs queries, holds logic, validates inline |
| Service | Business rules, transactions, events, jobs | Touches `Request`, writes queries |
| Repository | All Eloquent / DB queries, eager loading | Decides business rules |
| Resource | Shapes JSON / Inertia response | Fires queries (use `whenLoaded()`) |

## Controller pattern

Keep methods thin — 3 to 5 lines.

```php
public function store(StoreProductRequest $request): JsonResponse
{
    $product = $this->service->create($request->validated());

    return $this->success(new ProductResource($product), 'Product created', 201);
}
```

**Never:**
- `Model::where()`, `Model::query()`, `DB::` in a controller
- `$request->validate([...])` inline — use a FormRequest
- Return raw model or array — use a Resource

## Service pattern

```php
class ProductService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $repository
    ) {}

    public function create(array $data): Product
    {
        return DB::transaction(function () use ($data) {
            $product = $this->repository->create($data);
            ProductCreated::dispatch($product);

            return $product;
        });
    }
}
```

- Inject the **interface**, not the concrete class.
- Accept `array` (from `$request->validated()`), not the `Request` object.
- Transactions here, events here, jobs here.

## Repository + auto-binding

- Extend `BaseRepository`. Implement `{Name}RepositoryInterface`.
- All `with(...)` eager loading lives in the repository.
- Never return a query builder — only Models, Collections, or Paginators.

**Naming contract (required for auto-binding):**

| Type | Namespace | Suffix |
|---|---|---|
| Interface | `App\Repositories\Interfaces` | `RepositoryInterface` |
| Implementation | `App\Repositories\Eloquent` | `Repository` |

`AppServiceProvider::register()` scans these and binds them automatically — don't write manual `bind()` calls.

## Routes

### Verbs

- `PATCH` for edit-form updates (our default).
- `POST` for non-CRUD actions / state changes.

```
POST  /orders/{order}/cancel        ✅  correct
PATCH /orders/{order}               ❌  hides intent
POST  /posts/{post}/publish         ✅  correct
```

### Paths

- Plural, kebab-case: `/order-items`.
- Route params match model name: `{product}`, not `{id}`.
- Dot-notation names: `products.index`, `admin.products.update`.
- Nest at most one level.

### Split files by URL prefix

```
routes/
├── web.php                    ← thin loader
├── api.php                    ← mounts v1
├── web/
│   ├── products.php           ← /products/*
│   └── admin.php              ← /admin/*
└── api/v1/
    ├── auth.php
    └── products.php
```

Thin loader applies `prefix`, `as`, and middleware at `require`:

```php
// routes/web.php
Route::middleware(['auth', 'verified'])->group(function () {
    require __DIR__ . '/web/products.php';
});
```

```php
// routes/web/products.php
Route::prefix('products')->as('products.')->group(function () {
    Route::get('/', [ProductController::class, 'index'])->name('index');
    Route::post('/', [ProductController::class, 'store'])->name('store');
    Route::patch('/{product}', [ProductController::class, 'update'])->name('update');
    Route::delete('/{product}', [ProductController::class, 'destroy'])->name('destroy');
});
```

## Exception handling

Laravel 11+: all exception handling lives in `bootstrap/app.php` via `->withExceptions()`. Do not recreate `app/Exceptions/Handler.php`. Do not add `try/catch` in controllers just to change the response.

- Services and repositories `throw`. Controllers don't catch.
- Every domain exception extends `App\Exceptions\BusinessException`.
- Never `throw new \Exception('...')` in feature code.

```php
// app/Exceptions/BusinessException.php
class BusinessException extends Exception
{
    public function __construct(string $message = '', int $code = 400)
    {
        parent::__construct($message, $code);
    }
}
```

```php
// In a service
if ($product->stock < $quantity) {
    throw new ProductOutOfStockException($product->sku);
}
```

All API errors use the same envelope:

```json
{ "success": false, "message": "...", "errors": { } }
```

## Naming

| Thing | Rule | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Controllers | Singular + `Controller` | `ProductController` |
| Models | Singular PascalCase | `OrderItem` |
| Tables | Plural snake_case | `order_items` |
| Foreign keys | `{model}_id` | `user_id` |
| FormRequests | Action + Model + `Request` | `StoreProductRequest` |
| Resources | Model + `Resource` | `ProductResource` |
| Services | Model + `Service` | `ProductService` |
| Repositories | Model + `Repository` / `Interface` | `ProductRepository` |
| URIs | Plural kebab-case | `/order-items` |
| Route names | Dot notation | `products.index` |
| Booleans | `is / has / can` prefix | `is_published` |
| Events | Past tense | `ProductCreated` |
| Jobs | Imperative | `SendInvoiceEmail` |

## PHP style

- PSR-12, PHP 8.3+, `declare(strict_types=1);` on new files.
- Type everything (params, return, properties).
- Constructor property promotion, `readonly`, enums, match.
- Never call `env()` outside `config/*`.
- Run `./vendor/bin/pint` before committing.

## Frontend (Inertia + React + Tailwind v4)

- TypeScript everywhere. Shared types in `resources/js/types/index.ts`.
- Pages: `resources/js/Pages/{Module}/{Index,Create,Edit,Show}.tsx`.
- Use `useForm`, `Link`, `router` from `@inertiajs/react` — never hand-rolled `fetch` for Inertia navigation.
- Tailwind v4 is CSS-first: tokens in `resources/css/app.css` under `@theme { }`.
- Extract a component when the same utility string appears 3+ times.
- Use `cn()` / `clsx` for conditional classes.

## N+1 prevention

Add a relation field to a Resource → update the repository's eager loads in the same commit. Resources use `whenLoaded()` so a missing eager load surfaces as missing data (not a silent N+1).

## Anti-patterns — reject these in reviews

- `Model::where(...)` in a controller or service
- Inline `$request->validate([...])`
- Returning a raw model or array from a controller
- Services type-hinting concrete repositories instead of interfaces
- Eager loads in the controller
- Business logic inside a FormRequest or Resource
- `env()` outside `config/*`
- Recreating `app/Exceptions/Handler.php`
- `try/catch` in a controller to reshape responses
